{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>There</b> — And the meaning: they will fall in the place where they plotted to cast me down there, before they come to me. And some say: when the foot runs to come to me, it will stumble, and when the hand grows strong to cast me down, they will be pushed away, as in <i>דחה דחיתני לנפול</i> (You thrust me thrust to fall). And the meaning of 'there' is like 'then,' and similar to it: <i>שם יצעקו ולא יענה</i> (there they will cry out and He will not answer). And it is possible that 'there' is an allusion to the place where workers of iniquity fell there in days of old. And the meaning as I understand it: that the hand of the wicked will not cast me down, for they themselves will fall as those like them fell in time past."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:52.270050071Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}